.Dd June 26, 2026
.Dt BLUEDCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bluedctl
.Nd control utility for the blued Bluetooth Low Energy daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl ij
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Op Fl j
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm monitor
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm keyboard Ar addr
.Nm
.Fl i
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Nm
.Cm help
.Op Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is a command-line client for the
.Xr blued 8
Bluetooth Low Energy daemon.
It uses
.Xr libble 3
to issue typed, correlated operations over the daemon's Unix domain
control socket.
.Pp
In one-shot mode,
.Nm
sends a single command, prints the response, and exits with status 0
on success or 1 on error.
.Pp
In interactive mode
.Pq Fl i ,
.Nm
presents a prompt and accepts commands continuously.
Asynchronous events from the daemon (such as notification data and
passkey requests) are displayed as they arrive.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl i
Enter interactive mode.
Commands are read from standard input with a
.Dq Li bluedctl>
prompt.
Type
.Cm quit ,
.Cm exit ,
or press Ctrl-D to exit.
.It Fl j
Emit machine-readable JSON output: one JSON object per result or event,
suitable for scripting.
.It Fl s Ar socket
Connect to the specified Unix domain socket path instead of the default
.Pa /var/run/blued.sock .
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "unsubscribe"
.It Cm scan
Scan for nearby BLE devices.
The daemon performs a 5-second LE scan on all active adapters and
returns discovered devices.
.It Cm list
List currently connected BLE devices with their connection state and
HCI handle.
.It Cm status
Display daemon status including the number of active adapters and
connections.
.It Cm adapters
List active Bluetooth adapters with their names and addresses.
.It Cm adapter-caps Op Ar index
Display the selected adapter's power state and LE Read Local Supported Features
bitmask.  Check it before requesting optional controller procedures.
.It Cm connect Ar addr Op Cm public | Cm random
Initiate a BLE connection to the device with the specified Bluetooth
address.
The optional address type defaults to
.Cm public .
.It Cm disconnect Ar addr
Disconnect the device with the specified address.
.It Cm pair Ar addr
Check bond status for the specified device.
.It Cm bonds
List all bonded devices from the bond database.
.It Cm unbond Ar addr
Remove the bond for the specified device.
.It Cm services
List the local GATT database, showing all services and characteristics.
.It Cm discover Ar addr
Run GATT service discovery on a connected remote device.
.It Cm read Ar addr handle
Read a GATT characteristic value from a connected remote device.
The
.Ar handle
is specified in hexadecimal (e.g.,
.Li 0x0003 ) .
.It Cm write Ar addr handle hex
Write a value to a GATT characteristic on a connected remote device.
The
.Ar handle
is specified in hexadecimal, and
.Ar hex
is the value as a hexadecimal string.
.It Cm subscribe Ar addr handle
Subscribe to notifications for a characteristic on a connected remote
device.
In one-shot mode,
.Nm
stays connected and streams notification events until interrupted
with Ctrl-C.
.It Cm unsubscribe Ar addr handle
Unsubscribe from notifications for a characteristic.
.It Cm set-value Ar handle hex
Update the value of a local GATT attribute.
.It Cm add-service Ar uuid
Add a new service to the live local GATT database.
.It Cm add-char Ar svc_handle uuid props perms Op Ar value_hex
Add a characteristic to an existing local GATT service.
The
.Ar svc_handle
is the handle of the parent service,
.Ar props
are the characteristic properties,
.Ar perms
are the attribute permissions, and the optional
.Ar value_hex
sets the initial value.
.It Cm gatt-begin
Begin an atomic local GATT database update.
Subsequent add/remove operations are staged until committed.
.It Cm gatt-commit
Commit a staged local GATT database update atomically.
.It Cm gatt-rollback
Abort a staged local GATT database update.
.It Cm remove-service Ar handle
Remove a service and all its attributes from the local GATT database.
.It Cm loglevel Op Ar level
Get or set the daemon log level (0\(en5).
Without an argument, returns the current level.
.It Cm phy
Display PHY information (1M, 2M, or Coded) for all active connections.
.It Cm hogp-read Ar addr report_id
Read a Feature report from a connected HOGP (HID over GATT) device.
.It Cm hogp-write Ar addr report_id hex
Write a Feature report to a connected HOGP device.
.It Cm passkey Ar addr passkey
Reply to a passkey input request from the SMP pairing process.
This command is only useful in interactive mode
.Pq Fl i ,
where the
.Dq Li EVENT PASSKEY_INPUT
line is received asynchronously before the reply can be sent.
.It Cm confirm Ar addr Cm yes | Cm no
Reply to a numeric comparison request during SMP pairing.
This command is only useful in interactive mode
.Pq Fl i ,
where the
.Dq Li EVENT NUMCMP_REQUEST
line is received asynchronously before the reply can be sent.
.It Cm ecbfc-connect Ar addr psm count
Open Enhanced Credit Based Flow Control channels to a connected device.
.It Cm ecbfc-reconfig Ar addr mtu mps
Reconfigure ECBFC channel parameters.
.It Cm eatt-open Ar addr count
Open one to five daemon-owned EATT bearers on an encrypted LE connection.
.It Cm eatt-close Ar addr
Close all daemon-owned EATT bearers for the connection.
.It Cm iso-cig Ar cig_id Ar key=value ... Ar cis=id,msdu_c,msdu_p,phy_c,phy_p,rtn_c,rtn_p
Configure a Connected Isochronous Group and one or more CIS parameter sets.
Required group keys include
.Ar sdu_int_c ,
.Ar sdu_int_p ,
.Ar lat_c ,
and
.Ar lat_p .
.It Cm iso-cis Ar addr cig_id cis_id Op Cm push
Create a Connected Isochronous Stream to a peer from a configured CIG.
.It Cm iso-big Ar big_handle adv_handle Ar key=value ...
Create a Broadcast Isochronous Group for a local advertising handle.
.It Cm iso-big-sync Ar big_handle sync_handle Ar bis=list Op Ar key=value ...
Synchronize to a Broadcast Isochronous Group.
.It Cm iso-teardown-cis Ar handle Op Ar reason
Teardown a CIS.
.It Cm iso-remove-cig Ar cig_id
Remove a configured CIG.
.It Cm iso-accept Ar handle
Accept a pending peripheral CIS request.
.It Cm iso-reject Ar handle Op Ar reason
Reject a pending peripheral CIS request.
.It Cm iso-terminate-big Ar big_handle Op Ar reason
Terminate a local BIG.
.It Cm iso-big-terminate-sync Ar big_handle
Terminate BIG synchronization.
.It Cm adv-set-create
Allocate an extended advertising set owned by this control connection.
Handle zero is reserved for the primary advertising API.
.It Cm adv-set-params Ar handle props-hex min max Op Ar primary secondary
Configure event properties, intervals and optional PHYs for an owned set.
.It Cm adv-set-data Ar handle hex
Set the complete advertising payload for an owned set.
.It Cm adv-set-enable Ar handle Cm on | Cm off
Enable or disable an owned set.
.It Cm adv-set-remove Ar handle
Disable and remove an owned set.
Sets are also removed automatically when
their owning client disconnects.
.It Cm battery Ar addr
Read the battery level from a connected device by auto-discovering the
Battery Service (UUID 0x180F) and reading the Battery Level
characteristic (UUID 0x2A19).
Returns the battery percentage.
.It Cm devinfo Ar addr
Read device information from a connected device by auto-discovering the
Device Information Service (UUID 0x180A) and reading all available
characteristics (manufacturer name, model number, serial number,
hardware/firmware/software revision, system ID, PnP ID).
.It Cm heart-rate Ar addr
Read the heart rate measurement from a connected device by auto-discovering
the Heart Rate Service (UUID 0x180D) and reading the Heart Rate Measurement
characteristic.
.It Cm thermometer Ar addr
Read the temperature measurement from a connected device by auto-discovering
the Health Thermometer Service (UUID 0x1809) and reading the Temperature
Measurement characteristic.
.It Cm time Ar addr
Read the current time from a connected device by auto-discovering the
Current Time Service (UUID 0x1805) and reading the Current Time
characteristic.
.It Cm find Ar addr
Trigger a high alert on a connected device by writing to the Immediate
Alert Service (UUID 0x1802).
Useful for locating misplaced BLE peripherals.
.It Cm bond-export
Export the bond database in a text format suitable for diagnostics
and backup.
Each bonded device is listed with its address, address type, and
key flags (LTK, IRK, CSRK, Secure Connections, MITM protection).
.It Cm connparams Op Ar addr
Display connection parameters (interval, latency, supervision timeout)
for all active connections, or for a specific device if
.Ar addr
is provided.
.It Cm conninfo Op Ar addr
Display per-connection information including the connection handle,
role, negotiated ATT MTU, encryption state, and connection parameters,
for all active connections or for a specific device.
.It Cm advertise Cm on | Cm off
Enable or disable LE advertising.
Requires
.Xr blued 8
to have been started in peripheral mode.
.It Cm per-adv-params Ar min max Op properties
Configure periodic advertising for advertising set zero. Intervals are in
1.25 ms units. The adapter must advertise the periodic-advertising LE feature.
.It Cm per-adv-data Ar hex
Set up to 252 bytes of periodic advertising data.
.It Cm per-adv-enable Cm on | Cm off
Enable or disable periodic advertising after its parameters and data are set.
.It Cm per-sync-create Ar addr public|random sid Op skip timeout
Request synchronization to a peer's periodic advertising train. Completion and
reports arrive in monitor mode as EVENT PER_ADV_SYNC and EVENT PER_ADV_REPORT.
.It Cm per-sync-cancel
Cancel a pending periodic synchronization request.
.It Cm per-sync-terminate Ar handle
Terminate an established periodic synchronization.
.It Cm per-adv-list-add Ar addr public|random sid
Add a periodic advertiser to the controller list.
.It Cm per-adv-list-remove Ar addr public|random sid
Remove a periodic advertiser from the controller list.
.It Cm per-adv-list-clear
Clear the controller periodic-advertiser list.
.It Cm per-adv-list-size
Read the controller periodic-advertiser-list capacity.
.It Cm path-loss Ar addr low low-hyst high high-hyst min-time Cm on | Cm off
Configure controller path-loss threshold reporting for a connected peer.  The
adapter must advertise the path-loss-monitoring LE feature.
.It Cm past-transfer Ar peer service-data sync-handle
Transfer an established periodic synchronization to a connected peer using
Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer (PAST).  The adapter must advertise the
PAST sender feature.
.It Cm past-receive-enable Ar sync-handle Cm on | Cm off
Allow or reject a PAST received for an established synchronization.  The
adapter must advertise the PAST recipient feature.
.It Cm past-set-info-transfer Ar peer service-data adv-handle
Transfer synchronization information for a local periodic advertising set.
Nonzero advertising handles must be owned by this client.
.It Cm past-params Ar peer mode skip timeout cte-type
Set PAST receive policy for an established peer connection.
.It Cm past-default-params Ar mode skip timeout cte-type
Set the PAST receive policy inherited by future connections.
.It Cm adv-data Ar hex
Set the advertising data payload (up to 31 bytes) from a hex string.
.It Cm scan-resp Ar hex
Set the scan-response data payload (up to 31 bytes) from a hex string.
.It Cm monitor
Subscribe to push events and print them live until interrupted:
connection up/down
.Pq Dq Li CONNECTED , Dq Li DISCONNECTED ,
pairing prompts, and notifications.
This is the live view for the keyboard-pairing workflow.
.It Cm keyboard Ar addr
Pair a keyboard end-to-end in one command: connect to
.Ar addr ,
answer any passkey or numeric-comparison prompt interactively, and
report when the keyboard is connected and paired.
After pairing, keystrokes flow through the system HID stack.
.It Cm help Op Ar command
Print a command summary, or detailed usage for
.Ar command .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Scan for nearby BLE devices:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl scan
.Ed
.Pp
Connect to a device using a random address type:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl connect aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff random
.Ed
.Pp
Discover services on a connected device:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl discover aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff
.Ed
.Pp
Read a characteristic value:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl read aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff 0x0003
.Ed
.Pp
Subscribe to notifications and stream them:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl subscribe aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff 0x0025
.Ed
.Pp
Set the log level to 3 (debug):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl loglevel 3
.Ed
.Pp
Use interactive mode:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl -i
bluedctl> status
STATUS adapters=1 connections=0
bluedctl> scan
SCANNING
DEVICE [ubt0] aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff random rssi=-45 name=MyDevice mfr=0x004C
END
bluedctl> quit
.Ed
.Pp
Use a custom socket path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl -s /tmp/blued-test.sock status
.Ed
.Pp
Pair a keyboard and start typing
.Pq the Dq pair my keyboard and type No workflow :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl scan			# find the keyboard's address
# bluedctl keyboard aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff
Connecting to aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff ...
Enter the passkey shown on the keyboard: 123456
Connected to aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff (handle=0x0005, MTU=247).
Keyboard is ready \(em it now types into this system via the HID stack.
.Ed
.Pp
Alternatively, watch events live in one terminal while driving the
connection from another:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# bluedctl monitor &
# bluedctl connect aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff
CONNECTED    aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff  handle=0x0005 mtu=247
PASSKEY      aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff  device needs a passkey; reply with: ...
# bluedctl passkey aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff 123456
.Ed
.Sh PROTOCOL
.Nm
communicates with
.Xr blued 8
through
.Xr libble 3
using the daemon's versioned binary protocol.
Each operation carries a request identifier, typed domain and typed payload;
the daemon echoes the request identifier in its structured result.
Typed asynchronous events may arrive at any time and are displayed
immediately in interactive mode.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
maps the daemon's structured error taxonomy onto distinct exit codes so
scripts can react without scraping text:
.Bl -tag -width "0" -compact -offset indent
.It Li 0
Success.
.It Li 1
Generic or daemon error.
.It Li 2
Invalid arguments.
.It Li 3
Device not connected or not found.
.It Li 4
Permission denied (the command requires a privileged peer).
.It Li 5
Rate limited or an operation is already in progress.
.It Li 6
Timed out waiting for a response.
.El
.Pp
On error a short actionable hint is printed to standard error.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/blued.sock" -compact
.It Pa /var/run/blued.sock
Default control socket for communication with
.Xr blued 8 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bluetooth 3 ,
.Xr libble 3 ,
.Xr blued 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
